  c) <with|font-series|bold|<math|f<rsub|c><around*|(|x|)>=x e<rsup|-r x >>>.
  On suppose <math|r\<neq\>0>. En effet, si <math|r=0>,
  <math|f<around*|(|x|)>=x>, c'est une fonction linéaire ordinaire.

  cas particuliers <math|r=1> et r=-1

  <math|f<around*|(|x|)>=x e<rsup|-x>> et <math|g<around*|(|x|)>=x e<rsup|x>>

  <math|f=u\<times\>v> <math|f<rprime|'>=u<rprime|'>v+u v <rprime|'>>

  <math|f<rprime|'><around*|(|x|)>=1\<times\>e<rsup|-x>+x\<times\><around*|(|-e<rsup|-x>|)>=e<rsup|-x><around*|(|1-x|)>>

  <math|f<rprime|''><around*|(|x|)>=-e<rsup|-x>\<times\><around*|(|1-x|)>+e<rsup|-x>\<times\><around*|(|-1|)>>=<math|e<rsup|-x><around*|(|-1<around*|(|1-x|)>-1|)>>

  <math|=e<rsup|-x><around*|(|-2+x|)>> du signe de <math|x-2>

